fajita: SDM845 USB device mode from bergamota (Poco F1)

ry-diffusion/bergamota (https://github.com/ry-diffusion/bergamota) is an
ios-sweet fork on the same xnu-8796 base for the Poco F1, also SDM845. Its
iOS 16-era USB work (patches 0084-0110, 0094 citing anonbeat1/ios-sweet for
the apps_smmu bank) is taken as is, board checks widened from the Poco F1
to every SDM845 board (sweet_board_sdm845(): qcom,sdm845 in the ADT):
- keep the bootloader GCTL/DEVSPD, no DWC3 soft reset on SDM845 (the QMP
  SuperSpeed PHY that the reset needs is never restarted)
- UTMI clock as PIPE clock, GUCTL1 force-2.0-clock, sdm845 quirks
- QUSB2 POWER_DOWN fix on by default (sweetusbfix=0 turns it off)
- apps_smmu stream 0x740 on an identity-mapped bank (sweet_smmu.c)
- bus reset handling, ECM speed notification, SweetNetwork (ue0 at
  192.168.7.2 for configd)
The SDM845 GCC branch offsets from fajita 0082 are kept (bergamota still
reads the SM7150 ones).

