+/*
+ * EXPERIMENT (boot-arg sweetusbfix, off by default): the likely missing steps
+ * before the first endpoint command on the Poco F1.
+ *
+ * Evidence: DEPSTARTCFG (a pure register command) completes, DEPCMD
+ * SETEPCONFIG (which writes the endpoint's context RAM, clocked from the
+ * UTMI/PHY side) stays at 0x401 forever, whatever GCTL/reset variant is
+ * used. Every boot log's end-of-start QUSB2 dump reads PWR_CTRL1 = 0x23:
+ * POWER_DOWN (bit 0) is SET. ABL powers the HS PHY down when it hands over,
+ * and the earlier attempts (0084-0098) all assumed "PHY set up by ABL". With
+ * the PHY powered down there is no UTMI clock and the core cannot finish
+ * a command that touches its endpoint RAM. Linux phy-qcom-qusb2.c clears
+ * PWR_CTRL1.POWER_DOWN (after init) and waits for the PLL; dwc3 core_init
+ * then runs the full core reset (GCTL.CORESOFTRESET + both PHYSOFTRST bits,
+ * 100 ms, then DCTL.CSFTRST) and applies the dis_u1/u2-entry and
+ * parkmode-disable-ss quirks mainline's sdm845 DT sets.
+ *
+ * sweetusbfix=1 enables everything; any other value is a bit mask:
+ *   1 QUSB2 power-up (clear PWR_CTRL1.POWER_DOWN, wait for PLL lock)
+ *   2 Linux dwc3_core_soft_reset sequence + DCTL.CSFTRST (forces do_reset)
+ *   4 HS-only quirks: GUCTL1.PARKMODE_DISABLE_SS, DCTL INITU1/U2ENA = 0,
+ *     GUSB2PHYCFG.SUSPHY/ENBLSLPM = 0
+ */
+#define QUSB2_PWR_CTRL1         0x210
+#define QUSB2_PLL_STATUS        0x1a0
+#define QUSB2_PWR_DOWN          0x01u
+#define QUSB2_CLAMP_N_EN        0x02u
+#define QUSB2_PLL_LOCKED        0x20u
